Chapter: CheckersWasm
  cites Games chapter Checkers
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Checkers, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Sixty-four cells plus the turn and the verdict
 are past what an i32 could carry, so the page holds the board's address.

 `apply-move` writes the from square, the captured square and the to square
 through `list-set-at`, which mutates in place, so `ck-wasm-apply` copies
 first. The move GENERATOR does not need the copy: `generate-moves` builds
 its list by pushing onto an accumulator and `ck-score-move` reads the
 move's own fields rather than applying it, which is why asking this engine
 for a move does not corrupt the board it is asked about (GAME-13). The
 grader measures that rather than trusting this paragraph.

 A move is offered to the page as an INDEX into the generated list, with
 its from, to and captured squares readable, so the page can draw the legal
 destinations without knowing a rule of checkers.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  ck-copy-cells : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ck-copy-cells (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 64 then acc
    else ck-copy-cells src (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  ck-copy-board : CheckerBoard -> CheckerBoard
  ck-copy-board (b) =
    CheckerBoard {
      cells = ck-copy-cells (b.cells) 0 [],
      turn = b.turn,
      over = b.over,
      winner = b.winner
    }

Section: The Browser Interface

  ck-wasm-new : CheckerBoard
  ck-wasm-new = checkers-new 0

  ck-wasm-cell : CheckerBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ck-wasm-cell (b) (sq) =
    if sq < 0 then (-1)
    else if sq >= 64 then (-1)
    else list-at (b.cells) sq

  ck-wasm-turn : CheckerBoard -> Integer
  ck-wasm-turn (b) = b.turn

  ck-wasm-done : CheckerBoard -> Integer
  ck-wasm-done (b) = if b.over then 1 else 0

  ck-wasm-winner : CheckerBoard -> Integer
  ck-wasm-winner (b) = b.winner

  ck-wasm-movecount : CheckerBoard -> Integer
  ck-wasm-movecount (b) = list-length (generate-moves b)

  ck-wasm-move-from : CheckerBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ck-wasm-move-from (b) (i) =
    let ms = generate-moves b
    in if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length ms then (-1)
    else (list-at ms i).from-sq

  ck-wasm-move-to : CheckerBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ck-wasm-move-to (b) (i) =
    let ms = generate-moves b
    in if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length ms then (-1)
    else (list-at ms i).to-sq

  ck-wasm-move-cap : CheckerBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ck-wasm-move-cap (b) (i) =
    let ms = generate-moves b
    in if i < 0 then (-2)
    else if i >= list-length ms then (-2)
    else (list-at ms i).captured

  ck-wasm-apply : CheckerBoard, Integer -> CheckerBoard
  ck-wasm-apply (b) (i) =
    let ms = generate-moves b
    in if b.over then b
    else if i < 0 then b
    else if i >= list-length ms then b
    else apply-move (ck-copy-board b) (list-at ms i)

  ck-wasm-ai : CheckerBoard -> Integer
  ck-wasm-ai (b) =
    if b.over then (-1)
    else checkers-ai-move b 0

